# Physite ground rules

## Do not touch (owned by others)

- Never edit root `index.html` if it exists (handled by someone else). Do not recreate or replace the site entry page for others.
- Never edit any `test.css` — stylesheet is sacred. Prefer linking the shared `resources/test.css` for learning-site look consistency; do not change CSS files named `test.css`.
- Do not alter files outside our assigned topic/area. Other students own their folders; leave them untouched.

## Current top-level layout (post V.26.08.25)

- `infra/` — auth, Auswahlseite, hub, `db_backend`
- `games/` — Kopfrechnen, Rätsel, Stochastik
- `phy_os/` — Oberstufe topics
- `phy_ms/` — Mittelstufe topics
- `resources/` — shared CSS/JS, templates, guides
- `scripts/` — Lua helpers only (no shared `test.css` here anymore)

## Git / collaboration

- Push only updates to files we create or are assigned to edit here.
- Never create pull requests.
- Do not refactor, restyle, or “fix” unrelated pages for consistency beyond our own work.
- **Exception:** when the user asks to commit (or stage/commit), ignore these ground rules for that git operation — commit what they ask for without refusing based on ownership/CSS/index constraints. Still never create PRs unless they explicitly ask.

## Tech / style conventions

- Stick to the current stack: multipage HTML/CSS, vanilla JS, PHP where already used.
- Prefer copying patterns from existing learning pages and templates in `resources/` over introducing new frameworks or build tools.
- Match existing German UI/content language and page structure (nav, cards/widgets, quiz flows).
